  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enhancing Anti-Corruption in Liberia - Liberia Anti-Corruption and Integrity - new strategy 2021-2025</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">F&#xF6;rst&#xE4;rkt Anti-korruption i Liberia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Corruption is endemic within the Liberian society. The growing trend of public sector corruption has crippled Liberia&#x2019;s governance mechanisms, weakened the rule of law, impaired service delivery and undermined active citizens&#x2019; participation in the larger democratic governance process. 

The intervention&apos;s objective and various activities are directly addressing corruption in line with the national priorities in particular Pillar 4 (Governance) of the Pro Poor Agenda for Prosperity and Development (PAPD) and in particular the priority area on Reducing Corruption.

The anticipated results of the programme are threefold: 1) To Increase Citizens&#x2019; Access to Relevant Information to Demand and Take Actions Against Corruption; 2) To Increase strategic advocacy efforts of anti-corruption and promote good governance; and 3) To Strengthen the Capacity of the Center for accountability and Transparency in Liberia (CENTAL) to effectively lead the civil society voice against Corruption in Liberia.

The first year of implementation will be an inception phase. The inception phase will include milestone achievements to be realized during the year, and would also provide an opportunity for CENTAL to design a robust and forward-looking programme document and accompanying results framework and budget, conclude an action plan for the implementation of the recommendations from the systems audit, re-structure the board of CENTAL so that it reflects diversity and inclusivity and recruiting key staff such as a gender officer.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Korruptionen &#xE4;r vitt utbredd i det liberiska samh&#xE4;llet. Den &#xF6;kande trenden med korruption i den offentliga sektorn har p&#xE5;verkat samh&#xE4;llsstyrningen negativt, f&#xF6;rsvagat r&#xE4;ttsstatsprincipen, f&#xF6;rs&#xE4;mrat tillhandah&#xE5;llandet av samh&#xE4;llstj&#xE4;nster och underminerat aktiva medborgares deltagande inom demokratisk samh&#xE4;llsstyrning.

Insatsens m&#xE5;l och aktiviteter syftar till att motarbeta korruption i enlighet med prioriteringarna i den nationella utvecklingsagendan och det prioriterade sakomr&#xE5;det vilket &#xE4;r att motarbeta korruption i samh&#xE4;llet.

Programmets f&#xF6;rv&#xE4;ntade resultat &#xE4;r: 1) Att &#xF6;ka medborgarnas tillg&#xE5;ng till relevant information f&#xF6;r att kr&#xE4;va och vidta &#xE5;tg&#xE4;rder mot korruption; 2) Att &#xF6;ka fr&#xE4;mjandet av antikorruption bland medborgarna samt god samh&#xE4;llsstyrning; och 3) Att st&#xE4;rka kapaciteter hos Center for Transparency and Accountability in Liberia (CENTAL) f&#xF6;r att effektivt leda det civila samh&#xE4;llets r&#xF6;st mot korruption i Liberia.

Det f&#xF6;rsta &#xE5;ret kommer genomf&#xF6;ras med en inledningsfas, s.k. inception-fas. Fasen kommer omfatta milstolpar som skall genomf&#xF6;ras under f&#xF6;rsta &#xE5;ret, ge en m&#xF6;jlighet f&#xF6;r CENTAL att utveckla ett robust programdokument, resultatramverk samt budget, f&#xE4;rdigst&#xE4;lla en plan f&#xF6;r genomf&#xF6;rande av rekommendationerna fr&#xE5;n systemrevisonen, omstrukturera CENTAL&apos;s styrelse s&#xE5; den reflekterar m&#xE5;ngfald och inklusivitet samt att CENTAL kan rekrytera personal d&#xE4;ribland en j&#xE4;mst&#xE4;lldhetsr&#xE5;dgivare.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Goal:
A Corruption-free Liberia where Citizens Act with Transparency and Integrity in All their Dealings.
Specific Objectives: 1. To Increase Citizens&#x2019; Access to Relevant Information and Mechanisms to Demand for and Take Actions Against Corruption by December 2024;
2. To Increase Advocacy for Prevention and Prosecution Efforts Against Corruption by December 2024; and
3. To Strengthen the Capacity of CENTAL to effectively play her independent monitoring and advocacy roles by December 2024.</narrative>
  </description>
